            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During the walkthrough, we found leakage on the following items:

-Small leakage from the basement windows and the patio door		

-Receptacles

-Fireplace chimney

-Furnace

We recommend the installation of weather strippings around doors and receptacles to increase the airtightness of this components. 

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>We recommend to upgrade the garage section insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standards of R-28.</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>At the moment of the assessment, the attic insulation was R-30, and the garage section R-0. We recommend the addition of insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60.</ceilings>
                <windows>We recommend upgrading your basement window for Energy-star certified products. </windows>
                <VentilationSystem>According to the results, your natural ventilation airflow is not enough to ensure proper ventilation. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified, to compensate for the lack of ventilation. </VentilationSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>Have you already thought about having a heat pump. This system can use 3 times less energy for heating. Unfortunately, this kind of heating system requires a secondary heating system to ensure heating in the cold season when the temperature is lower than 250C. However, a heat pump could work with the existing furnace using the existing ductwork and relying on the furnace to ensure heating when the outdoor temperature is too cold. </HeatingSystem>
                <WaterConservation>We recommend to upgrade your existing toilet for a low flow toilet to reduce your water consumption. </WaterConservation>
            </RURComments>
